{
    "background_story": "Leif was a gentle giant, a gray whale belonging to the Eschrichtiidae family. He roamed the Pacific coast, migrating thousands of miles each year to reach his favorite feeding grounds. Leif's massive body glided effortlessly through the ocean, his baleen plates filtering tiny crustaceans and plankton from the water. Despite his enormity, he was a curious creature, often approaching whale-watching boats to inspect the humans who came to marvel at him. Leif's annual migrations became a celebrated event in coastal towns, with locals gathering to bid him farewell and welcome him back. His gentle nature and predictable routes made him a beloved ambassador for his species, inspiring a new generation of ocean stewards and conservationists.",
